  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO&apos;s tripartite constituents must address global and regional geopolitical turbulence that affects economic and social stability. Globally connected employers in Africa need an environment that supports private sector growth, job creation and fair wages. The mid-term review of the Abidjan Declaration Plan 2019 shows progress on local infrastructure and business projects, but highlights the need for better social dialogue and capacity building for employers&apos; organisations. Key priorities include flexible labour regulations, investment attraction, skilled labour permits, infrastructure and talent mobility. Skills development is essential for sustainable development and competitiveness. The ILO must adapt its implementation of the Abidjan Declaration to changing needs, emphasizing social dialogue in crisis response and recovery.</narrative>
  </description>
